  "conclusion": "The speculative final K16 prefetch caused out-of-bounds reads; remaining faults were TMU word reads beyond the final FP16 scale. Buffer inventory located all three remaining addresses exactly at allocated scale-buffer ends. Re-reading the last valid K16 and aligned word/half selection removes all observed MMU errors across the same six model cases and 840 compute dispatches, preserving numerical outputs. This is bounded validation, not sustained driver reliability."
